{
  "_comment": [
    "The watchlist. Employer ATS boards first, aggregators second.",
    "Reading an employer's own board is the highest-signal source there is: if the",
    "posting is on the company's board today, the search is live. That is what the",
    "`signal` field in CONTRACT.md is for.",
    "To find a company's token, open their careers page and read the URL:",
    "  job-boards.greenhouse.io/TOKEN     -> type greenhouse",
    "  jobs.ashbyhq.com/TOKEN             -> type ashby",
    "  jobs.lever.co/TOKEN                -> type lever",
    "  apply.workable.com/TOKEN           -> type workable",
    "  jobs.smartrecruiters.com/TOKEN     -> type smartrecruiters",
    "VERIFIED LIVE on 2026-08-03. Every enabled employer row below was requested",
    "against its ATS endpoint on that date and returned HTTP 200 with at least one",
    "posting, and the board's own name was checked so a token could not be a",
    "different company with the same word in it. That last check matters: ashby",
    "`runway` is cfo.ai, not Runway ML, so Runway ML is disabled rather than wrong.",
    "A token is not a promise about tomorrow. Boards move ATS, so re-run",
    "`python3 ingest/fetch_jobs.py --only greenhouse --only ashby --only workable`",
    "when a familiar employer goes quiet: a moved token prints one FAIL line with an",
    "HTTP 404 and the run continues.",
    "Set enabled to false rather than deleting, so the watchlist stays readable. The",
    "disabled employer rows are companies worth watching whose token could not be",
    "confirmed. Each one records what the endpoint actually returned, so the next",
    "person does not re-guess the same misses.",
    "See SOURCES.md for why LinkedIn and Indeed are not in this list."
  ],

